      <div type="clause" n="10.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> 10.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.2" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="240" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ænig man heonan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.2-2"/> forð cyrican ne ðeowige, ne cyricmagunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.star"/> mid unriht ne macie, ne cyricþen ne utige butan biscopes geþehte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.2" corresp="#wit-g2"><pb n="240" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ ænig man heonan forð cyrican ne þeowige, ne cyricmagunge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.1"/> mid unrihte ne macige, ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.2"/> cyricþen ne utige butan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.3"/> biscopes geþehte.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.2" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="241" ed="#liebermann"/>And æni man heonan forð cirican ne ðeowige, ne ciricmangunge mid unrihte ne macyge, ne ciricðen ne utige buton biscopes geþeahte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="10.2" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="82" ed="#robertson"/>And æni man heonan forð cirican ne ðeowige, ne ciricmangunge mid unrihte ne macyge, ne ciricðen ne utige buton biscopes geþeahte.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="150" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And ænig man heonan forð cyrican ne ðeowige, ne cyricmangunge mid unriht ne macie, ne cyricþen ne utige butan biscopes geþehte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="241" ed="#liebermann"/>Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.1"/> niemand unterwerfe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.2"/> hinfort eine Kirche einer Dienstpflicht oder treibe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.3"/> gesetzwidrig mit Kirchen Handel oder vertreibe ohne des Bischofs Beistimmung einen Kirchendiener [den angestellten Priester<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.4"/>].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let no one henceforth subject a church to servitude, or unlawfully traffic in churches, or expel a church-servant [the appointed priest] without the bishop's consent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d"><ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.1"/><pb n="83" ed="#robertson"/>And no-one henceforth shall oppress<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.2"/> the church, or make it an object of improper traffic<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.3"/>, or turn out a minister of the church without the bishop's consent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="449" ed="#whitelock"/>And no man henceforth is to bring a church under subjection, nor illegally to traffic with a church,<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#VAtr_10-2.whinote.n.2"/> nor to expel a minister of the church without the bishop’s consent.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g"><pb n="151" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And henceforth no one shall persecute the church, nor wrongfully make it an object of exchange, nor expel a cleric without the bishop’s permission.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="241"><ref target="clause:Wi_1">Wi 1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. Wi. 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘cyricmagunge’ should be corrected to ‘-mangunge’ from D and VI Atr 15. Liebermann compares Wi 1.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cyricmangunge: cyricmagunge G1G2</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">240</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">240</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">später</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e later</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">240</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">tan <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">tan written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">240</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">verb. aus</hi> hon.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">corr. from hon.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">240</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> -mangunge <hi rend="italic">aus D VI Atr.</hi> 15</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read -mangunge from D VI Atr. 15</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= VI 15, benutzt Northu 20—22</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= VI 15, used by Northu 20—22</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Eigentlich ‘versklave’. Trinoda necessitas (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2) lastete normal auf der Kirchenfreiheit; <hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3; Geistliche 12. 27; Bischof 5e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Literally ‘enslave’. The trinoda necessitas (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2) normally lay upon church immunity; <hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3; Geistliche 12. 27; Bischof 5e</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘simony’ richtig Toller</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Toller rightly has ‘simony’</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">172</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So Northu 22; sonst ‘Altardiener’. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Degradation 2a; Eigenkirche 2; Pfarre 7b</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So Northu 22; elsewhere ‘servant of the altar’. Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Degradation 2a; Eigenkirche 2; Pfarre 7b</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.1" n="1" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Cf. VI Atr. 15; <hi rend="italic">N.P.L.</hi> 20–22.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.2" n="2" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Lit. ‘enslave.’ Liebermann suggests that lay patrons may have been in the habit of subjecting ecclesiastical foundations to secular duties, and quotes the case of Crediton, which in 739 became <hi rend="italic">causarum fiscalium, rerum regalium, saecularium operum immunis</hi> (see Napier and Stevenson, <hi rend="italic">Crawford Charters</hi>, p. 2).</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.robnote.n.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">‘Simony’ (see BT. p. 156, <hi rend="italic">s.v. ciricmangung</hi>), cf. Anselm (1102): <hi rend="italic">ne ecclesiae aut praebendae emantur</hi>. Lay abbots were common in Scotland in the eleventh century.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="VAtr_10-2.whinote.n.2" n="2" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">449</biblScope></bibl><label>church</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Not merely simony, but the bartering of churches such as that complained of by Ælfric, <hi rend="italic">Lives of Saints,</hi> I, 430, where he says men deal with churches as with mills.</seg></note>
      </div>
